        <!-- Closing CTA -->
        <div class="mt-16 bg-gray-900 text-white rounded-2xl p-8">
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-white mb-4">The Bottom Line</h2>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            <strong class="text-white">Clip the key, straddle the belt, start slow.</strong> Step on
            only once the belt is moving at its lowest speed, build up gradually, let go of the
            rails once you are steady, and stop by slowing down first and stepping off only when
            the belt has come to rest.
          </p>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            Keep the first week short and conversational, add incline in small steps, and run with
            shorter, quicker strides while looking ahead. When the routine is automatic, our
            <a href="/treadmill-workouts/" class="text-[#5AA9FF] font-bold no-underline">treadmill workouts guide</a>
